computing/src/scheme/prologue

This directory contains the Turing machine simulator, turing-machine.rkt,
written in Racket.

The directory machines/ contains various Turing machines used in the text
and the exercises.

Note also the presence of a unit tester for those machines, at
computing/bin/turing_machine/tm_test.py.  And, there are scripts
to convert the input to output.  Notably, in
computing/bin/turing_machine is a Python program used by the Makefile in
/computing/src/prologue/asy/tm_exercises to get
the .pdf outputs used in the text and exercises.


RUNNING A SIMULATION

To run a machine, write a file, say machines/even_charfcn.tm, and
then use a command line like this.

ftpmaint@millstone:~/Documents/computing/src/scheme/prologue$ ./turing-machine.rkt -f machines/even_charfcn.tm -c "1" -r "111111" -s 100

Here, -c is the character under the head, -r is the tape to the right of the
head, -l is the tape to the left of the head, and -s is a limit on the number
of steps the machine performs.